--- !u!114 &1968963990
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1968963989}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8a106443188e67b4ba994b8c9de70deb, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FrameLab.FrameLabInspection
  parts:
  - id: lining
    title: "01 \xB7 Internal lining"
    shortName: Lining
    description: The plasterboard forms the room-side finish. This cutaway leaves the opening visible. Compare its position with the timber frame, then rotate the assembly to see the return at the window.
    surface: {fileID: 1811811384}
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 60c347ad1a16cfb4d8bfa12217232b67, type: 3}
  - id: frame
    title: "02 \xB7 Timber rough opening"
    shortName: Timber
    description: The studs, sill and head frame the opening and support the surrounding wall. Follow the vertical members to see where loads travel. Isolate this part to examine the complete rough opening.
    surface: {fileID: 1811811383}
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: ae8f03cb9412b394ba95820b1dcff8da, type: 3}
  - id: wrap
    title: "03 \xB7 Wall wrap"
    shortName: Wrap
    description: The wrap sits outside the timber frame, behind the cladding. It forms part of the wall's weather protection. Look at how the opening interrupts this layer and where the flashings meet it.
    surface: {fileID: 1811811382}
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b60114feb94c3d64181e4f956cc01f9f, type: 3}
  - id: sill
    title: "04 \xB7 Sill flashing"
    shortName: Sill
    description: This flashing sits beneath the window. Its upstand and outward projection illustrate a drainage path away from the opening. Isolate it and rotate the model to see the folded shape.
    surface: {fileID: 1811811381}
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e00f930eecadbfd45b4e7670634274fa, type: 3}
  - id: jamb
    title: "05 \xB7 Jamb flashing"
    shortName: Jambs
    description: These strips protect the sides of the opening. Compare their lower ends with the sill flashing. The installation sequence and overlaps are important to a continuous drainage path.
    surface: {fileID: 1811811380}
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d18f20063ddc6cd44b1154b615ecac07, type: 3}
  - id: window
    title: "06 \xB7 Window frame"
    shortName: Window
    description: The aluminium frame surrounds and holds the glazing. Inspect the head, sill and side members. This is a schematic frame; individual fixings, packers and drainage slots are not represented.
    surface: {fileID: 1811811379}
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 57488cbf53d219a47aebdd733a6dcb49, type: 3}
  - id: glass
    title: "07 \xB7 Glazing"
    shortName: Glass
    description: The glass fills the window frame while admitting light and views. The blue tint makes this thin component easier to locate in the study. Isolate it to see its outline and thickness.
    surface: {fileID: 1811811378}
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c35256b8f76390248901ac7196c15858, type: 3}
  - id: head
    title: "08 \xB7 Head flashing"
    shortName: Head
    description: The head flashing protects the top of the opening. Its outward projection helps direct water away from the window. Rotate it to compare its shape with the sill flashing below.
    surface: {fileID: 1811811377}
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7a04ab6c9b8ecc84fbdbe178515f4f38, type: 3}
  - id: brick
    title: "09 \xB7 Brick veneer"
    shortName: Veneer
    description: The outer brick leaf forms the exterior face. This cutaway exposes the layers behind it. Notice the separation between the brickwork and timber wall; the brick leaf is distinct from the timber frame.
    surface: {fileID: 1811811376}
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 754f13a37147e194fbc3dd5e02fb71b5, type: 3}
  grab: {fileID: 1968963991}
--- !u!114 &1968963991
